{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1419445-is-pennywise-a-beast-or-slasher","id":1419445,"title":"Is Pennywise a beast or slasher.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-21T14:47:42-07:00","id":1419445,"title":"Is Pennywise a beast or slasher.","content":"no idea what lessons he teaches but.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T14:51:43-07:00","id":1419449,"title":"","content":"Insatiable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T15:22:12-07:00","id":1419457,"title":"","content":"Agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T15:44:10-07:00","id":1419466,"title":"","content":"I will remind you PotN that lessons are unnecessary for a Beghotten to actually function, its just something a number of Beasts do.<br /> <br /> I don't know Slashers. so can't say anything about that. I am with Satchel and Penelope though in that It/Pennywise/The Deadlights/Bob Gray/The Spider is probably closer to an Insatiable than one of the Beghotten. The fears it operate on tend to be more irrational, note in the book it attacked as a werewolf and the giant claw at one point, and that part of its function in Derry seems to have been the near complete apathy towards the events going on and some other things. Add in that the shapeshifting and occasionally dragging through of monster into the flesh state isn't something a Beghotten's atavisms actually do in that manner and you've got more of a leaning towards the Insatiables and their moments as opposed to Beghottens even at the level of Incarnates.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T16:39:48-07:00","id":1419478,"title":"","content":"I'll buck the trend slightly:<br /> <br /> Pennywise is an Unfettered Horror. My primary reasoning for this (since it's not like a high powered Unfettered and an Insatiable are that different to deal with) is that Pennywise is still very connected to humanity in a way the Insatiable generally aren't. As a former Begotten, a lot of how It functions makes sense as a being that used to be a high Lair Beast who was killed using the Ritual of Chud while Slumbering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T16:42:10-07:00","id":1419479,"title":"","content":"I tend to be a fan of the cosmic horror aspect of Pennywise (Spider, Turtle, Dark Tower, and all that) and so my CofD translation for IT always makes me pick Idigam as my favorite choice, but gotta agree Insatiable is a valid alternative.<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, for a shameless self-promotion, here's this thing I wrote back when the first of the recent IT movies happened: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1227908-it-pennywise-the-idigam\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ise-the-idigam</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 10-21-2020, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T17:30:28-07:00","id":1419485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1419445-is-pennywise-a-beast-or-slasher?p=1419479#post1419479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to be a fan of the cosmic horror aspect of Pennywise (Spider, Turtle, Dark Tower, and all that) and so my CofD translation for IT always makes me pick Idigam as my favorite choice, but gotta agree Insatiable is a valid alternative.<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, for a shameless self-promotion, here's this thing I wrote back when the first of the recent IT movies happened: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1227908-it-pennywise-the-idigam\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ise-the-idigam</a></div> </div> </div> </div>A point I often wonder about, but seldom commented upon by Stephen King fans, is the similarity between Pennywise and Rose Madder, making me wonder if she was, at least something very much like that creature, if not the same thing.<br /> <br /> Edit: Could a case be made for Pennywise as one of The Gentry?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26456-van-owen","user":"Van Owen","date":". 10-21-2020, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26456-van-owen","name":"Van Owen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T18:15:49-07:00","id":1419493,"title":"","content":"These are all good ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T03:29:35-07:00","id":1419548,"title":"","content":"Now, murderclowns as a concept is not that uncommon, but the form Pennywise usually takes is that of a genuine clown and there is something inherently contradictory in a creature in a form supposed to inspire laughter to feed on fear. Thus Pennywise/It could work as a Gulmoth that is weak to being forced into recognisable narratives/story tropes by the main characters.<br /> <br /> My preferred take would still be a Beast/Insatiable, but it doesn't mesh well with the Pennywise/It dichotomy. They're definitely the same creature in one way or another, but they're also two different manifestations of that creature. For It as an ephemeral being, Pennywise could definitely be some type of Royal Avatar (or possibly Herald in case of an Idigam), but afaik nothing like that exists in BtP. But it's far from the game I know the best so I might be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T05:40:12-07:00","id":1419561,"title":"","content":"The form of Pennywise and It in general makes sense in a Beast context as an Inguma (closely followed by Namtaru). Their whole thing is the fear of the other... which is the core theme of the story. The whole point of Pennywise is to be a form that's unusual enough to draw a bit of attention from potential victims, but seems safe and fun until it's too late.... something the Inguma excel at.<br /> <br /> As for the ephemeral being part, that's why I brought up It being an Unfettered Horror. At some point It's human body was killed, leaving the Horror free to operate as an ephemeral being. A Beast with a high Lair rating and perhaps the Legendary Horror Merit can easily end up with a Rank 4+ Unfettered Horror that still has a human-ish intelligence. Its Ban is related to its Hunger before the Inheritance kicked in, thus it maintains the Pennywise manifestation, and if the original Beast died with the Ritual of Chud as an Anathema on it, it would get incorporated into the Unfettered's Bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T20:01:14-07:00","id":1419699,"title":"","content":"Couldnt it also be an incarnate though? Pennywise has not only the Myth, but also the power and flexibility (and yet, inflexibility due to upholding the Myth) to be a particularly successful Inarnate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T21:01:22-07:00","id":1419706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1419445-is-pennywise-a-beast-or-slasher?p=1419699#post1419699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldnt it also be an incarnate though? Pennywise has not only the Myth, but also the power and flexibility (and yet, inflexibility due to upholding the Myth) to be a particularly successful Inarnate</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd considered that, but the problem is Pennywise isn't really a known entity. There aren't any legends or rumors about the clown or any of its forms, save legends pertaining to forms it steals from an individuals fears, Derry isn't really aware It exists and since it lacks tendrils or a connection outside Derry, that does kind of hinder the master of its own Legend thing for Incarnates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T03:36:29-07:00","id":1419756,"title":"","content":"That was my thinking as well when considering a Begotten that had reached on of the Inheritances as well.<br /> <br /> The idea that people that leave Derry quickly forget about It is very rough of the Myth side of things. It prefers to corrupt the town unseen to ensure it stays a perfect feeding ground rather than exposing Its nature directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T06:10:55-08:00","id":1557594,"title":"","content":"He's a Beast. I believe it's explicitly pointed out that he can't harm you if you aren't scared of him. That's why he sets up mind games with his prey before going for the feast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T14:56:48-08:00","id":1557621,"title":"","content":"He actually can harm people that aren't scared of him, it just doesn't really benefit him and very few things are such a threat to him that he would waste the energy to harm them to no benefit to himself. He gets physical with the adult Losers Club precisely because they've become a risk by overcoming their fear of him and he tries to directly harm them to demoralize them before they can weaponize their lack of fear against him fully (though books vs. miniseries vs. movies varies things a bit there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T23:10:43-08:00","id":1558176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1419445-is-pennywise-a-beast-or-slasher?p=1557621#post1557621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He actually can harm people that aren't scared of him, it just doesn't really benefit him and very few things are such a threat to him that he would waste the energy to harm them to no benefit to himself. He gets physical with the adult Losers Club precisely because they've become a risk by overcoming their fear of him and he tries to directly harm them to demoralize them before they can weaponize their lack of fear against him fully (though books vs. miniseries vs. movies varies things a bit there).</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I misinterpreted the scene of him helping that guy escape the mental ward. IT made it seem like he needed the guy's help, since the Losers weren't scared anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T00:39:20-08:00","id":1558177,"title":"","content":"The novel is the only place where ITs recruitment of Henry Bowers is really explained (and even then, not really explicitly). Because he's basically just a normal human, Henry can be scary in a way that IT can't be; just letting go of fear doesn't stop Henry from hurting you like it can stop IT temporarily. The novels also imply that Henry is more possessed than anything else, as he taps into the shroud of fear that makes adults in Derry constantly ignore what's going on in their town. Instead of attacking Eddie in the shower like in the movie, he attacks Eddie in the middle of the day in front of the main shops in town with lots of witnesses (and isn't defeated even if driven off). Many of them start to move to intervene before magically getting compelled to not get involved. And him being protected that way happens more than once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}